#DESCRIPTION
Hybrid PIC (kinetic ions / fluid electrons) Proton Cyclotron Anisotropy
Instability (PCAI) wave test.

1D-3V: the ion temperature is anisotropic (bi-Maxwellian) with
  T_perp/T_par = 3, beta_par = 1,
so the plasma exceeds the proton-cyclotron anisotropy instability threshold
  P_perp/P_par - 1 ~ S / beta_par^0.4   (S ~ 1)
and a left-hand circularly-polarized (Alfven/ion-cyclotron) wave grows parallel
to the guide field at the linear-theory rate gamma/Omega_ci = 0.162.  This
validates the hybrid solver's capture of an electromagnetic anisotropy
instability driven by ion free energy (no net current / beam).

The anisotropic distribution is seeded by the WAVEIC anisoTPerpOverTPar option:
the UNIFORMSTATE temperature T is interpreted as the PARALLEL temperature T_par,
and the WaveIC thermal-velocity hook inflates the two components perpendicular
to the guide field (x) by sqrt(T_perp/T_par) = sqrt(3).  The initial state has
NO E or B field perturbation (frac = 0): only the uniform guide field plus the
pressure/temperature anisotropy.  The instability therefore grows purely from the
anisotropic ion free energy and the ~1% thermal-noise floor, without a seeded
B_y/B_z mode.  The growth rate is measured from the total transverse-field norm
sqrt(sum(By^2)) / sqrt(sum(Bz^2)) in tests/pcai/validate.py.

Normalization is chosen for a clean time conversion: lNormSI = uNormSI = 1.0e5
  so tNorm = 1.0 s and TimeMax == T_code == t*Omega_ci directly (dt = 0.01 s
  gives dt*Omega_ci = 0.01).  The guide field gives B_code ~ 1 (Omega_ci = 1):
  bx = 1.044e-8 T (Omega_ci(SI) = eB/m_p = 1 rad/s); v_A ~ 1.02 (not set to 1).
Physical inputs: n = 5 /cc, B = 10.44 nT, v_A ~ 102 km/s,
T_par ~ 6.28e5 K (beta_par = 1), T_perp = 3 T_par.

The box is Lx = 10.5 d_i, 64 cells (dx = 0.164 d_i); the box-fundamental
k d_i = 2*pi/10.5 = 0.598 lies in the unstable band of the parallel
proton-cyclotron mode and the box holds one growing wavelength (waveMode = 1).
Run to t*Omega_ci = 40 (TimeMax = 40 s), long enough to grow from the
thermal-noise floor and saturate (~0.24); fields saved every 500 steps (~8
frames inside the growth window [0.2, 0.85]*amp_max for a reliable fit).

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-5.25                   xMin  [code units; Lx = 10.5 d_i]
 5.25                   xMax
-0.05                   yMin
 0.05                   yMax
-0.05                   zMin
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
1                       nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
64                      maxBlockSizeX
1                       maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

#SOLVEEM
F                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
T                       useHybridPIC

#AVGFIELDB
F                       useAvgFieldB
20                      nAvgFieldB

useAvgFieldB = F disables FLEKS's EMA time-averaging of B (reference uses no
B time-averaging).

#RESISTIVITY
0.0                     etaResistivity  [m^2/s, SI magnetic diffusivity]

Warm massless fluid electrons with T_e = T_par (54.2 eV = 6.28e5 K), adiabatic
index gamma = 5/3.  Cold electrons (Te = 0) do not produce the instability (the
n=1 mode just oscillates), while warm electrons, whose pressure-gradient term
couples to the parallel density perturbation of the parallel proton-cyclotron
mode, do drive the growth.
#ELECTRONTEMPERATURE
54.2                    electronTemperature  [eV]  (T_e = T_par = 6.28e5 K)
1.6667                  electronGamma             (5/3)
1.0                     electronDensity0

Charge-density floor for the 1/rho factors in the Hall term and the
electron-pressure-gradient term.  The reference clamps rho at max(rho, 0.05);
raising the floor from the default (1e-6) to 0.05 prevents (J x B)/rho and
grad(Pe)/rho from blowing up if the density dips locally in the high-amplitude
nonlinear phase.
#MINIMUMDENSITY
0.05                    rhoMinOhm

#BSUBCYCLE
1                       nBSubcycle

Time-integration for the hybrid Faraday (B) update.  "rk4" evaluates E at the
time-centred B (B_stage + B^n)/2 in the generalized Ohm's law at each stage.
#FIELDINTEGRATOR
rk4                     fieldIntegrator

Single kinetic ion species (q = m = 1); the electron is an implicit
neutralizing massless fluid, so no electron particle species is present.
#PLASMA
1                       nSpecies
1.0                     mass
1.0                     charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions (n = 5 /cc)
0.0                     ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
6.28e5                  T [K]        T_par (beta_par = 1; B doubled so T ~ B^2)
1.044e-8                bx [T]       guide field Bx0 (B_code~1, Omega_ci(SI)=1)
0.0                     by [T]
0.0                     bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
0.0                     ey [V/m]
0.0                     ez [V/m]

#TESTCASE
hybridwave

#WAVEIC
1                       waveMode            box-fundamental unstable mode
0.0                     frac                NO B perturbation (matches reference)
3.0                     anisoTPerpOverTPar  T_perp/T_par anisotropy ratio

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.01                    dt            dt*Omega_ci = 0.01

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]  ~ d_i so d_i ~ 1 in code units
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s] tNorm = lNormSI/uNormSI = 1.0 s
                                          (v_A ~ 1.02 in code units; NOT 1 --
                                           only tNorm = 1 matters here)

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
10                      dnSavePic
10                      dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
600                     nParticle per cell in X   (reduced for a ~1-min run)
1                       nParticle per cell in Y
1                       nParticle per cell in Z

#COMOVING
F                       solvePartInCoMov
0                       nSmoothBackGroundU

#UPWINDE
F                       useUpwindE
0.0                     limiterThetaE

#UPWINDB
F                       doSmoothB
0.0                     theta

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 fluid ascii pic     plotString
500                     dn
-1                      dt
1                       dx

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
40.0                    TimeMax      t*Omega_ci = 40 ~ 6.4 gyro-periods (tNorm=1)

#RUN
